{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe completion-verification close gate still fails to close legitimately complete tickets: the verifier agent trips the runaway-tool-loop guard (RunawayToolLoopError) while re-reading evidence files, the gate aborts, and authors are pushed toward `--force` — the exact symptom bug 46a2-9c1a-d855-4706 set out to eliminate.\n\nPrior art (this plan builds ON it, not around it): epic 9b71 shipped the windowed distinct-ratio runaway guard (breaker/detector). Epic 10ae/story 2948 then shipped three levers in src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py: (1) completion-policy evidence banking, (2) a path-normalized read_file memo (`_memo_toolsets`) that reads a whole file once and serves subsequent range requests by slicing the cache, (3) large-file summarize/cap handling. The loop persisted DESPITE the memo layer.\n\nRoot cause (confirmed by reading the live composition in agent_call.py): the guard sits OUTERMOST (layer-order pinned Guard→Memo→Steering), so it observes every call BEFORE the memo layer answers it. A memo-SERVED repeat — free, harmless, exactly what lever 2 was built to produce — is therefore still counted as loop evidence by the guard's distinct-ratio window. Lever 2 made repeats cheap; the guard still punishes them: the two shipped fixes fight each other. Secondary defect in the same composition: reads past the cached window fall back to uncached exact-range reads, so long files degrade the ratio further.\n\n## Approach\nRecompose guard and memo via a SHARED ledger instead of reordering layers (the completion policy sits between them and must keep seeing calls). New module src/rebar/llm/runaway_guard.py: `ToolCallLedger` tracks observed vs EXECUTED calls plus a served-streak; the memo layer calls `record_executed` at each site that performs real work (non-allowlisted passthrough, exact-signature miss, read_file first-read, truncated-window fallback). The guard becomes two arms: (arm 1) the distinct-ratio computed over the EXECUTED stream only — memo-served repeats are no longer loop evidence; (arm 2) a served-streak backstop that still bounds a pure cache-served loop after a FULL window of consecutive zero-execution calls (checked at call entry, before increment). Guard stays outermost; layer order unchanged; completion policy unaffected. Governance-notice loops (policy answers without delegating) stay bounded by arm 2 since policy responses never reset the streak.\n\nOut of scope, filed as follow-up when this lands: tri-state evidence banking (BOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE banks met=false at search exhaustion — should bank insufficient_evidence), to be linked discovered_from this bug.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/llm/runaway_guard.py (new) — ToolCallLedger + two-arm guard.\n- src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py — memo layer records executed work into the ledger (4 sites); build_agent_kwargs creates one ledger per call and passes it to both layers; old in-file guard removed.\n- tests/unit/test_agent_call_memo_nudge.py — recomposition coverage.\n\n## Testing\n- Regression (withheld oracle, proven to FAIL on the old guard): a verifier pattern of 2 cached re-reads per novel call (i%3) must NOT trip the guard — memo-served repeats are not loop evidence for the ratio arm.\n- Backstop: a pure cache-served loop (zero execution for a full window) still trips, with the served-streak message text distinguishing the arm.\n- Non-allowlisted looping tool still trips the ratio arm (passthrough calls are executed work).\n- Error-looping allowlisted tool (responses never cached) still trips the ratio arm.\n- Layer-order test keeps pinning Guard→Memo→Steering.\n- Manual mutation pass over the new module and the 4 record_executed sites; every mutant killed (mutation testing already surfaced and filled 2 gaps: non-allowlisted loop, error-looping exact-sig path).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A verifier run that re-reads memoized evidence files completes without RunawayToolLoopError; checked by test_memo_served_repeats_are_not_loop_evidence_for_the_ratio_arm (fails on pre-fix code).\n- [ ] A genuine loop — non-allowlisted repeat, error-looping tool, or pure cache-served spin — is still bounded; checked by the three trip tests (both arms).\n- [ ] Layer order and completion-policy visibility unchanged; checked by the existing layer-order test staying green.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the LLM-area test suite green; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1) before close."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786686543339146001,"uuid":"abfd84eb-85d2-4d9b-8fc9-6dac86ca22e5"}